  "proof_route": [
    "Call the original actual lower-scale supplier on the dictionary hpair, yielding U,V >= X0^(1/4).",
    "Use actual X0=M*U*V and positive X0^(1/4) to cancel one long factor: M*U,M*V <= X0^(3/4).",
    "Use the original FixedScaleTransport at fixed epsilon=1/16000, preserving its actual Z and halfOrder X0: Y <= X0^(1/16000).",
    "Use old eventually_fixed_log_le_power with constant 2, degree 0, reserve 1/16. Thus the cross term is <= X0^(13001/16000) <= X0^(7/8).",
    "Use old eventually_pairCost_power_payment with reserve 1/8 and c=1 to pay the weighted cross term; actual natural block endpoints pay U,V in [1,X0].",
    "Use the published dominant PowerPayment and D>=1 to pay the weighted square term monotonically.",
    "For the bare terms, use old eventually_fixed_log_le_power with constant 1, degree extraLog+accuracy, reserve 1/8. Multiplication by the positive log denominator and the rpow addition identity give the exact desired log bound.",
    "Y <= X0^(1/16000) <= X0^(1/4) <= U <= U+V gives M*Y^2 <= M*(U+V)*Y, paying the bare square term.",
    "Combine all fixed real thresholds before N; kap0<1 and the existing physical trim lower bound N^(1-kap0)/64 < X0 pay T<=X0 uniformly before every row, tuple and historical parameter."
  ],
